  "proposed_scope": "Keep the historical snapshot and tied-HQ guard retention. Only relocate a short boundary return target inward for an alive, connected, assigned HQ guard currently outside the inset; retain stable target caching, entrance priority, ownership and departure gates.",
  "limitations": [
    "Recorded states and N+1 actual commands are observations; a changed request on these fixed states is not a new match, realized displacement, survival benefit or score improvement.",
    "At step 250 HQ blue=7 still fails the existing <=3 contested-departure gate. This dead zone alone does not explain the failure to depart or the final score.",
    "Navigation mesh and obstacle clearance are not exposed. An inward request still requires live validation; public geometry is not proof of traversability.",
    "The 200-280 interval mostly has movement and no local enemy detections for these units, so it does not establish attack interruption of clearance plans as the primary issue.",
    "The inset is stricter than the public capture box; outside the inset does not imply the engine excluded a unit from redTeamNum."
  ]
